wayland: a window opened with focus asks for the keyboard

`WindowOptions::focus` was dropped on Linux: a window opened in answer
to input took the keyboard only if the compositor gave it unasked, so a
slide show opened by F5 left its keys with the window behind (Ely R20.39).
The ask waits for the first commit: compositors skip unmapped surfaces.

diff --git a/vendor/gpui-pre-linux/src/linux/wayland/window.rs b/vendor/gpui-pre-linux/src/linux/wayland/window.rs
--- a/vendor/gpui-pre-linux/src/linux/wayland/window.rs
+++ b/vendor/gpui-pre-linux/src/linux/wayland/window.rs
